  "description": "FOJZAH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H75 Cl2 Er3 N12 O15 Zn2,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Zn1 (Zn) has 2 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 2 O neighbors; Er1 (Er) has 4 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.433-3.565 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.60-106.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn2(L)3Cl2(μ2-OH)(μ3-OH)2Er3(N3)2]·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
